### Vue.js `@click` Directive

In Vue.js, the `@click` directive is a shorthand for `v-on:click`. It is used to listen for click events on an element and execute a method or expression when the event occurs.

#### Basic Usage

```html
<template>
  <button @click="handleClick">Click Me</button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  methods: {
    handleClick() {
      console.log('Button was clicked!');
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

#### Explanation

- **`@click="handleClick"`**: This binds the click event to the `handleClick` method defined in the component's methods.
- **`handleClick` method**: This method is executed whenever the button is clicked.

#### Advanced Usage

You can also pass arguments to the method or use inline expressions:

```html
<template>
  <button @click="handleClick('Hello, World!')">Click Me</button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  methods: {
    handleClick(message) {
      console.log(message);
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

In this example, clicking the button will log "Hello, World!" to the console.

### Summary

- `@click` is a shorthand for `v-on:click`.
- It is used to bind click events to methods or expressions.
- It can pass arguments to the method or use inline expressions.

